      "sourceHash": "26cd12b530ae68e4d04bf51e25dfb51892b02c0132d26ce73082f313c95966b4",
      "cues": [
        {
          "id": 1,
          "start": 2.22,
          "end": 3.52,
          "en": "Now up to this point,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 2,
          "start": 3.52,
          "end": 7.32,
          "en": "I always just worked with my main Vue app here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 3,
          "start": 7.32,
          "end": 9.81,
          "en": "Typically, of course, you have multiple components.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 4,
          "start": 9.81,
          "end": 11.78,
          "en": "Let's say we have a separate component",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 5,
          "start": 11.78,
          "end": 13.7,
          "en": "for the user data here,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 6,
          "start": 13.7,
          "end": 16.505,
          "en": "so we could create a components folder,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 7,
          "start": 16.505,
          "end": 19.89,
          "en": "and in there have a UserData.vue file.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 8,
          "start": 19.89,
          "end": 21.57,
          "en": "And here in the template,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 9,
          "start": 21.57,
          "end": 26.477,
          "en": "I want to have my age two tag with the username.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 10,
          "start": 30.36,
          "end": 35.36,
          "en": "And I want to have my age free tag with my age.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 11,
          "start": 40.03,
          "end": 42.02,
          "en": "Now we can add a script here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 12,
          "start": 42.02,
          "end": 44.03,
          "en": "and we can expect some props here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 13,
          "start": 44.03,
          "end": 46.81,
          "en": "because that data should come from outside,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 14,
          "start": 46.81,
          "end": 48.1,
          "en": "username and age.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 15,
          "start": 48.1,
          "end": 52.573,
          "en": "So we could add a username and age prop here,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 16,
          "start": 53.48,
          "end": 57.05,
          "en": "and now simply go back to App.vue",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 17,
          "start": 57.05,
          "end": 60.25,
          "en": "and import this user data component",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 18,
          "start": 60.25,
          "end": 65.25,
          "en": "from ./components/UserData.vue,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 19,
          "start": 69.48,
          "end": 73.13,
          "en": "and register it with the components option.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 20,
          "start": 73.13,
          "end": 76.46000000000001,
          "en": "And as I mentioned before, you still have this option,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 21,
          "start": 76.46000000000001,
          "end": 78.53,
          "en": "this does not go into the setup method,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 22,
          "start": 78.53,
          "end": 80.58,
          "en": "you keep your option here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 23,
          "start": 80.58,
          "end": 83.75,
          "en": "So we register UserData here, this new component,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 24,
          "start": 83.75,
          "end": 86.32,
          "en": "and we can then use it here,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 25,
          "start": 86.32,
          "end": 90.49,
          "en": "user-data, opening and closing,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 26,
          "start": 90.49,
          "end": 93.61,
          "en": "and bind those props, userName and age.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 27,
          "start": 98.11,
          "end": 103.11,
          "en": "And I'll bind userName to my userName computed ref,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 28,
          "start": 104.15,
          "end": 108.06,
          "en": "which is exposed here in the return to object",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 29,
          "start": 108.06,
          "end": 112.87,
          "en": "to the template, and bind age to this age ref,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 30,
          "start": 112.87,
          "end": 114.263,
          "en": "which we're also exposing.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 31,
          "start": 115.72999999999999,
          "end": 119.82300000000001,
          "en": "And that, therefore, all just works, as you can tell.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 32,
          "start": 122.46,
          "end": 126.3,
          "en": "However, maybe we wanna do more in this component.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 33,
          "start": 126.3,
          "end": 130.67,
          "en": "Maybe here we wanna use the setup method as well,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 34,
          "start": 130.67,
          "end": 133.5,
          "en": "because maybe we don't get the userName like this,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 35,
          "start": 133.5,
          "end": 138.34,
          "en": "but instead we get the first name and last name separated,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 36,
          "start": 138.34,
          "end": 141,
          "en": "and we want to compute it here in the setup method.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 37,
          "start": 141,
          "end": 144.41,
          "en": "Well, first of all, let's maybe not use the setup method,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 38,
          "start": 144.41,
          "end": 146.98,
          "en": "but a good old computed option.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 39,
          "start": 146.98,
          "end": 150.05,
          "en": "So let's use the Options API here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 40,
          "start": 150.05,
          "end": 153.17000000000002,
          "en": "Then we could have a userName computed property,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 41,
          "start": 153.17000000000002,
          "end": 155.51,
          "en": "since that's what I'm using here in the template,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 42,
          "start": 155.51,
          "end": 159.827,
          "en": "and simply return this dot firstName + blank,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 43,
          "start": 159.827,
          "end": 164.18,
          "en": "+ this dot lastName, right?",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 44,
          "start": 164.18,
          "end": 165.68,
          "en": "This is how we could do this",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 45,
          "start": 165.68,
          "end": 169.04,
          "en": "in a regular component, using the Options API,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 46,
          "start": 169.04,
          "end": 171.6,
          "en": "if we get two props and we wanna merge it",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 47,
          "start": 171.6,
          "end": 173.063,
          "en": "into one computed prop.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 48,
          "start": 174.47,
          "end": 177.72,
          "en": "Now, we just need to bind first and last name.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 49,
          "start": 177.72,
          "end": 182.72,
          "en": "So in App.vue, I now bind first-name and last-name,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 50,
          "start": 184.13,
          "end": 188.24,
          "en": "and the values here should be my firstName ref",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 51,
          "start": 188.24,
          "end": 190.97,
          "en": "and my lastName ref.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 52,
          "start": 190.97,
          "end": 193.61,
          "en": "And we now need to ensure that both are exposed",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 53,
          "start": 193.61,
          "end": 194.93,
          "en": "to the template.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 54,
          "start": 194.93,
          "end": 197.77,
          "en": "The firsName ref already is,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 55,
          "start": 197.77,
          "end": 200.25,
          "en": "but the lastName ref is not anymore.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 56,
          "start": 200.25,
          "end": 203.23,
          "en": "So let's re add lastName to the object,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 57,
          "start": 203.23,
          "end": 205.32999999999998,
          "en": "which we are returning in setup,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 58,
          "start": 205.32999999999998,
          "end": 207.803,
          "en": "so that this is available in the template.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 59,
          "start": 208.89,
          "end": 213.89,
          "en": "And now firstName and lastName are forwarded to user data.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 60,
          "start": 214.31,
          "end": 219.13,
          "en": "And if I saved that, this just works,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 61,
          "start": 219.13,
          "end": 221.8,
          "en": "and this might or might not be a surprise,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 62,
          "start": 221.8,
          "end": 224.14,
          "en": "but there's a very important message here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 63,
          "start": 224.14,
          "end": 229.14,
          "en": "You can absolutely mix the Options and the Composition API.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 64,
          "start": 229.16,
          "end": 232.82,
          "en": "App.vue uses the Composition API.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 65,
          "start": 232.82,
          "end": 235.82,
          "en": "UserData.vue uses the Options API,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 66,
          "start": 235.82,
          "end": 239.57,
          "en": "and there is nothing wrong with it, absolutely nothing.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 67,
          "start": 239.57,
          "end": 243.54,
          "en": "Just because you used the Composition API in one component,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 68,
          "start": 243.54,
          "end": 245.56,
          "en": "does not mean you have to use it",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 69,
          "start": 245.56,
          "end": 248.08,
          "en": "in all components, it's optional.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 70,
          "start": 248.08,
          "end": 251.8,
          "en": "You can use it wherever it makes sense to you.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 71,
          "start": 251.8,
          "end": 255.7,
          "en": "So, it is absolutely fine to use the Options API",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 72,
          "start": 255.7,
          "end": 259.073,
          "en": "and therefore the computed option here, in UserData.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 73,
          "start": 260.47,
          "end": 263.21,
          "en": "And you'll see that those ref values",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 74,
          "start": 263.21,
          "end": 265.44,
          "en": "are extracted correctly by Vue,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 75,
          "start": 265.44,
          "end": 269.733,
          "en": "and forwarded as values for first and last name props.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 76,
          "start": 270.71,
          "end": 273.27,
          "en": "Nonetheless, even though we don't have to,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 77,
          "start": 273.27,
          "end": 276.8,
          "en": "let's say we wanna migrate to the Composition API",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 78,
          "start": 276.8,
          "end": 278.82,
          "en": "inside of UserData as well.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 79,
          "start": 278.82,
          "end": 281.4,
          "en": "So, instead of using computed here,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 80,
          "start": 281.4,
          "end": 286.4,
          "en": "we import computed from the Vue framework like this,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 81,
          "start": 287.76,
          "end": 290.463,
          "en": "and we then add our setup method.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 82,
          "start": 291.46,
          "end": 295.72,
          "en": "Here, we got our uName, let's say,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 83,
          "start": 295.72,
          "end": 297.64,
          "en": "of course, this name is up to you.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 84,
          "start": 297.64,
          "end": 300.9,
          "en": "And we derive it by calling computed",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 85,
          "start": 300.9,
          "end": 303.35,
          "en": "and passing a function to computed,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 86,
          "start": 303.35,
          "end": 307.66,
          "en": "where we now return, well return what?",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 87,
          "start": 307.66,
          "end": 309.98,
          "en": "We wanna get access to our props here,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 88,
          "start": 309.98,
          "end": 311.587,
          "en": "firstName and lastName.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 89,
          "start": 312.57,
          "end": 315.81,
          "en": "In the computed option, we did it with the, this keyword,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 90,
          "start": 315.81,
          "end": 318.95,
          "en": "but I can tell you, and I told you before,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 91,
          "start": 318.95,
          "end": 322.04,
          "en": "that this will not work like that.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 92,
          "start": 322.04,
          "end": 324.64,
          "en": "So if we try to use the, this, keyword",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 93,
          "start": 324.64,
          "end": 328.15,
          "en": "and get access to our props here, this won't work.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 94,
          "start": 328.15,
          "end": 329.71,
          "en": "We can still give it a try.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 95,
          "start": 329.71,
          "end": 333.42,
          "en": "Let's return username here as an object,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 96,
          "start": 333.42,
          "end": 336.12,
          "en": "and point at the computed uName property,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 97,
          "start": 336.12,
          "end": 339.806,
          "en": "so that in the template, userName is available,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 98,
          "start": 339.806,
          "end": 342.5,
          "en": "and let's save this.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 99,
          "start": 342.5,
          "end": 346.09000000000003,
          "en": "And you'll notice that I can reload and get an error,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 100,
          "start": 346.09000000000003,
          "end": 350.12,
          "en": "cannot read property firstName of undefined.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 101,
          "start": 350.12,
          "end": 353.65999999999997,
          "en": "So, trying to access firstName on this fails,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 102,
          "start": 353.65999999999997,
          "end": 357.243,
          "en": "because this is undefined at this point,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 103,
          "start": 358.23,
          "end": 361.81,
          "en": "because setup basically gets called too early by Vue.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 104,
          "start": 361.81,
          "end": 363.03,
          "en": "At this point of time,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 105,
          "start": 363.03,
          "end": 365.573,
          "en": "the Vue instance object, doesn't exist yet.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 106,
          "start": 367.47,
          "end": 370.04,
          "en": "So we don't have access to props like that.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 107,
          "start": 370.04,
          "end": 372.72,
          "en": "Still, of course, we do get access to props",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 108,
          "start": 372.72,
          "end": 375.322,
          "en": "because setup actually is a method",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 109,
          "start": 375.322,
          "end": 378.99,
          "en": "that accepts two arguments.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 110,
          "start": 378.99,
          "end": 383.17,
          "en": "The first parameter we get here, is the props parameter.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 111,
          "start": 383.17,
          "end": 385.53,
          "en": "It's an object full of the props",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 112,
          "start": 385.53,
          "end": 387.18,
          "en": "you're getting in this component.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 113,
          "start": 388.02,
          "end": 391.523,
          "en": "And therefore, you can simply access props.firstName,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 114,
          "start": 391.523,
          "end": 394.546,
          "en": "and props.lastName, like this.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 115,
          "start": 394.546,
          "end": 397.3,
          "en": "Now you can name this argument however you want,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 116,
          "start": 397.3,
          "end": 399.11,
          "en": "by the way, it's your method.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 117,
          "start": 399.11,
          "end": 402.06,
          "en": "So any name of your choice is fine,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 118,
          "start": 402.06,
          "end": 403.37,
          "en": "but I'll go with, props,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 119,
          "start": 403.37,
          "end": 406.76,
          "en": "and I'll stick to props throughout this course here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 120,
          "start": 406.76,
          "end": 409.08,
          "en": "And with that, if we saved it and reload,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 121,
          "start": 409.08,
          "end": 413.573,
          "en": "now it's working again, as you can tell.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 122,
          "start": 415.33,
          "end": 418.7,
          "en": "So, to setup method receives this props argument",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 123,
          "start": 418.7,
          "end": 421.56,
          "en": "automatically passed in by Vue.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 124,
          "start": 421.56,
          "end": 423.93,
          "en": "If your component gets no props,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 125,
          "start": 423.93,
          "end": 425.56,
          "en": "it's simply an empty object.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 126,
          "start": 425.56,
          "end": 427.48,
          "en": "You'll always get this props thing,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 127,
          "start": 427.48,
          "end": 430.83,
          "en": "but it can be empty if you don't have any props.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 128,
          "start": 430.83,
          "end": 432.627,
          "en": "Here we do have three props,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 129,
          "start": 432.627,
          "end": 436.32,
          "en": "and therefore they're all part of this props object.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 130,
          "start": 436.32,
          "end": 439.32,
          "en": "And whenever props should change from outside,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 131,
          "start": 439.32,
          "end": 443.26,
          "en": "this change is all propagated here to the setup method",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 132,
          "start": 443.26,
          "end": 445.92,
          "en": "and computed, for example, will pick up",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 133,
          "start": 445.92,
          "end": 449.71,
